<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf William, Duke of Saxe-Eisenach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1632">1632</a>–<a href="/years/1668">1668</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf William was a son of Duke William of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> as his own duchy when his father's lands were divided in 1662. He ruled it until his death in 1668. His only surviving son, William Augustus, was born after his death and died in 1671, ending the line, and Eisenach was then redistributed among the Ernestine dukes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolf-william-duke-of-saxe-eisenach.jpg" alt="Adolf William, Duke of Saxe-Eisenach" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Richter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolph_Wilhelm_Sachen-Eisenach_C._Richter@Weimar_Schlossmuseum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
